+## 5. {file.*} Config Value Expansion
+
+*Added: 2026-05-16*
+
+**Decision:** Support `{file.<path>}` placeholders in string config fields. The placeholder is replaced with the contents of the referenced file, with trailing `\r\n` stripped.
+
+**Rationale:** Secret values (e.g., API keys) should not be stored in plain-text config files. Referencing a secrets file (e.g., one managed by a password manager or stored in a restricted directory) lets users keep credentials out of `~/.lth/config.toml`. Stripping trailing newlines is essential because Unix convention causes most text editors and secret management tools to append a `\n` to file contents.
+
+**Consequence:** `expandFileRefs` is called in `Load` between TOML decoding and `applyDefaults`. Only the following string fields are expanded (explicit list, no reflection): `LLM.APIKey`, `LLM.BaseURL`, `LLM.Provider`, `LLM.Model`, `Embedding.BaseURL`, `Embedding.Provider`, `Embedding.Model`, `Embedding.DockerImage`, `DB.Path`, `Watcher.StateFile`, and each element of `Watcher.Paths`. `Load` propagates file-read errors to the caller.
+
+---
+
 ## 2. ~/.lth/ Home Directory Convention
 
