+**Scenario:** String with no {file.*} placeholder passes through unchanged.
+**Setup:** Call `expandFileRefsInString("no-refs-here")`.
+**Assertions:** Returns same string, no error.
+
+## TestExpandFileRefsInString_SimpleRef
+**Scenario:** {file.<path>} placeholder is replaced by file contents.
+**Setup:** Write a secret file; call `expandFileRefsInString("{file.<path>}")`.
+**Assertions:** Returns file contents with no trailing newline, no error.
+
+## TestExpandFileRefsInString_TrimsTrailingNewline
+**Scenario:** File ending with \n has newline stripped.
+**Setup:** Write file with content "value\n"; expand placeholder.
+**Assertions:** Returns "value" (no trailing newline).
+
+## TestExpandFileRefsInString_TrimsTrailingCRLF
+**Scenario:** File ending with \r\n has both characters stripped.
+**Setup:** Write file with content "value\r\n"; expand placeholder.
+**Assertions:** Returns "value".
+
+## TestExpandFileRefsInString_MissingFile
+**Scenario:** Placeholder referencing a non-existent file returns an error.
+**Setup:** Call `expandFileRefsInString("{file./nonexistent}")`.
+**Assertions:** Error returned.
+
+## TestExpandFileRefsInString_EmptyString
+**Scenario:** Empty string input is handled gracefully.
+**Setup:** Call `expandFileRefsInString("")`.
+**Assertions:** Returns "", no error.
+
+## TestLoadFileRef_LLMAPIKey
+**Scenario:** `{file.*}` in `[llm] api_key` is expanded on Load.
+**Setup:** Write secret file with "sk-ant-abc123\n"; write TOML referencing it; call `Load`.
+**Assertions:** `cfg.LLM.APIKey == "sk-ant-abc123"` (newline stripped).
